<title>USA: Brent steady to firmer in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent steady to firmer in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent was steady to firmer in late U.S. paper trading on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>A major Wall Street trader sold seven June partial cargoes to a mixed bag of players at between $17.72 and $17.75 a barrel.</p>
<p>The June contract on London's IPE settled at $17.72 a barrel.</p>
<p>May/June Brent fetched minus 31 and minus 34 cents a barrel, down from minus 30 earlier in the day.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
